             <div class="blog-body">
                <h1 class="blog-title text-center mb-4">NEET UG 2026 Admit Card &amp; Exam Details: Your Essential Guide to Success</h1>
                <p>The National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET UG) 2026 is a pivotal examination for lakhs of aspiring medical students across India. Conducted by the National Testing Agency (NTA), this entrance test is the gateway to undergraduate medical courses such as MBBS, BDS, BAMS, BHMS, and other allied programs in prestigious institutions nationwide. With the exam date officially set, candidates are eagerly awaiting crucial details, especially regarding the NEET UG 2026 Admit Card.</p>

                <p>As the competition intensifies each year, staying informed about the latest updates, application timelines, admit card release, and exam day guidelines is paramount for effective preparation and a smooth examination experience.</p>

                <div class="highlight-text">
                    <p><strong>NEET UG 2026 Exam Date: Sunday, May 3, 2026!</strong> Mark your calendars and intensify your preparation for this significant day.</p>
                </div>

                <h2 class="section-title">NEET UG 2026: Key Highlights at a Glance</h2>
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Particular</th>
                            <th>Details</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Examination Name</td>
                            <td>National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET UG) 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Conducting Body</td>
                            <td>National Testing Agency (NTA)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Official Websites</td>
                            <td>nta.ac.in, neet.nta.nic.in</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Exam Date</td>
                            <td>May 3, 2026 (Sunday)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Exam Mode</td>
                            <td>Offline (Pen-and-Paper, OMR-based)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Application Window</td>
                            <td>February 8, 2026 - March 11, 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Admit Card Release</td>
                            <td>Last week of April 2026 (Expected)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Result Declaration</td>
                            <td>Mid-June 2026 (Expected)</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>

                <h2 class="section-title">NEET UG 2026 Admit Card: Your Gateway to the Exam Hall</h2>
                <p>The NEET UG 2026 Admit Card is a mandatory document for all candidates appearing for the examination. Without it, entry to the exam hall will be strictly prohibited. It contains crucial personal and examination-related details. The NTA is expected to release the admit card in the last week of April 2026, approximately 10-15 days before the exam date, around April 29, 2026.</p>

                <div class="benefit-item">
                    <div class="benefit-title">City Intimation Slip: A Precursor to Your Admit Card</div>
                    <div class="benefit-content">
                        Before the official admit card, NTA will release the NEET 2026 City Intimation Slip. This slip informs candidates about their allotted examination city, helping them make necessary travel arrangements in advance. It is usually released around 10 days before the exam date and can be accessed on the official NTA NEET website using your application number and date of birth. The actual exam center address will only be available on the admit card.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="benefit-item">
                    <div class="benefit-title">How to Download Your NEET UG 2026 Admit Card</div>
                    <div class="benefit-content">
                        Once released, follow these simple steps to download your admit card:
                        <ol>
                            <li>Visit the official NTA NEET website: <a href="https://neet.nta.nic.in" target="_blank">neet.nta.nic.in</a>.</li>
                            <li>Look for the link labeled "Download NEET (UG) Admit Card 2026" on the homepage or in the 'Candidate Activity' section.</li>
                            <li>Click on the link, which will redirect you to a login page.</li>
                            <li>Enter your credentials: Application Number, Date of Birth, and the Security Pin (Captcha) displayed on the screen.</li>
                            <li>Click "Submit" to view your admit card.</li>
                            <li>Carefully verify all the details mentioned on the admit card.</li>
                            <li>Download and take at least two-three printouts on A4 size paper for future reference and exam day.</li>
                        </ol>
                        <p>In case of any discrepancies in the details on your admit card, contact the NTA authorities immediately.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="benefit-card">
                    <div class="benefit-title">✅ Essential Details on Your NEET UG 2026 Admit Card</div>
                    <p>Your admit card will contain crucial information including:</p>
                    <p>✅ Candidate's Name, Roll Number, and Application Number</p>
                    <p>✅ Father's and Mother's Name</p>
                    <p>✅ Date of Birth and Gender</p>
                    <p>✅ Photograph and Signature of the candidate</p>
                    <p>✅ Exam Date, Day, and Timing</p>
                    <p>✅ Examination Centre Name and Address</p>
                    <p>✅ Medium (Language) of the Examination</p>
                    <p>✅ Important Exam Day Instructions and Guidelines</p>
                </div>

                <h2 class="section-title">NEET UG 2026 Exam Details You Must Know</h2>
                <p>The NEET UG 2026 exam will be conducted in an offline, pen-and-paper (OMR-based) mode on May 3, 2026. Candidates must adhere to strict guidelines on the examination day.</p>

                <div class="benefit-card">
                    <div class="benefit-title">✅ Eligibility Criteria for NEET UG 2026</div>
                    <p>To be eligible for NEET UG 2026, candidates must meet the following criteria:</p>
                    <p>✅ Minimum age of 17 years by December 31, 2026.</p>
                    <p>✅ Must have passed or be appearing for Class 12 with Physics, Chemistry, Biology/Biotechnology, and English as core subjects.</p>
                    <p>✅ Minimum aggregate marks in PCB: 50% for General, 40% for OBC/SC/ST, and 45% for PwD categories.</p>
                    <p>✅ Indian Nationals, NRIs, OCIs, PIOs, and Foreign Nationals are eligible.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="benefit-item">
                    <div class="benefit-title">Important Instructions for Exam Day</div>
                    <div class="benefit-content">
                        <p>On the day of the examination, ensure you carry the following:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Printed copy of your NEET UG 2026 Admit Card.</li>
                            <li>One passport-size photograph (same as uploaded in the application form).</li>
                            <li>A valid original photo ID proof (Aadhaar Card, PAN Card, Voter ID, Passport, Driving License, etc.).</li>
                            <li>PwBD Certificate (if applicable).</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>Strictly avoid carrying any restricted items such as electronic devices, written material, wallets, handbags, belts, caps, sunglasses, metallic items, food items, or any communication devices inside the examination hall.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h2 class="section-title">Crucial Dates for NEET UG 2026 Aspirants</h2>
                <p>Keep track of these important dates to ensure you don't miss any critical deadlines:</p>
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Event</th>
                            <th>Date/Timeline</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>NEET UG 2026 Notification Release</td>
                            <td>January/February 2026 (Expected)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Online Application Start Date</td>
                            <td>February 8, 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Last Date to Apply Online</td>
                            <td>March 11, 2026 (9:00 PM)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Last Date for Fee Payment</td>
                            <td>March 11, 2026 (11:50 PM)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Application Correction Window</td>
                            <td>March 12 - 14, 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>NEET 2026 City Intimation Slip Release</td>
                            <td>Around April 23, 2026 (Approx. 10 days before exam)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>NEET UG 2026 Admit Card Release</td>
                            <td>Last week of April 2026 (Expected by April 29, 2026)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>NEET UG 2026 Examination Date</td>
                            <td>May 3, 2026 (Sunday)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>NEET UG 2026 Result Declaration</td>
                            <td>Mid-June 2026 (Expected)</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>

                <p>The NEET UG 2026 examination is a significant milestone in your academic journey. By staying updated with official announcements, understanding the application and admit card download process, and preparing diligently, you can confidently approach the exam. Remember to regularly check the official NTA websites (nta.ac.in and neet.nta.nic.in) for the latest and most accurate information. Good luck with your preparations!</p>
